# cards-gpu: what the two GPU cards (perf_card.py, rk78_card.py) import, plus the build
# backends the editable installs need (--no-build-isolation). CPython 3.12, Linux x86_64.
# CUDA runtime: 12.9 (PyTorch cu129 wheels and the nvidia-*-cu12 12.9 libraries they pin, NVRTC
# included, shared by CuPy and JAX): one runtime for every GPU from Turing (sm_75) to Blackwell
# (sm_120); JAX compiles with ptxas 12.9 to SASS. No PTX JIT on the timed paths.
# Driver floor: >= 575.51 (CUDA 12.9); an older CUDA 12 driver >= 525.60.13 may run it through
# minor-version compatibility, but only 575 and later is tested. A driver older than ptxas 12.9 only
# makes XLA warn and compile serially.
# GPU floor: compute capability 7.5 (the cu129 PyTorch wheel carries sm_75..sm_120, no sm_60/61/70).
# Pre-Turing GPUs (P100, V100, GTX 10xx; sm_60-sm_70): use `--cuda 12.6` (cards-gpu-cuda126.in).
--extra-index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu129
